WEBVTT

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:23.290
You're... a Witch.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.950
Witches must be hunted.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.600
Isn't that right, Amon?

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:45.030
I've hunted so many... believing that the Craft was a power meant to hunt Witches.

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.720
Let's have takoyaki again sometime, okay?

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.440
I'm gonna be Minori Yoshida starting today.

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:24.480
Wait!

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:40.420
I'll survive.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:45.230
I'll survive... as a Witch.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:59.470
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:05.200
...the instant I look away.

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:10.340
I just kept counting...

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:15.780
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:23.150
...that I'd vomited up.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:29.090
In this time that seems so dry,

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:34.200
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:40.060
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:43.110
...and tears them to pieces.

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:52.780
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:02:55.310 --> 00:03:00.610
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.650
Somebody who came into the country in the past month...

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.740
...through an American military base, huh?

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:45.690
I even tried going through the Immigration Bureau's data,

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:49.020
...but sure enough, I didn't get any hits on anybody fitting that description.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:50.920
Well, that's not surprising.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:53.600
Okay, you're on.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.960
It's risky work, but since it's you who's asking me to do it...

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.830
I owe you one.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.770
Guess I'll try my next snitch.

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:20.450
Are you busy?

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:23.220
No, come in.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.430
Do you have some new information?

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:31.370
There are only scraps of information relating to Amon,

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.130
...but they've apparently tracked him down.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.100
Amon, sir?

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:41.100
Yes. As we suspected, Amon's injuries were treated at Solomon headquarters.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:43.710
Which would suggest that he's in Europe now.

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:45.200
Yes...

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:48.550
As far as his wounds go, they've apparently completely healed already.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:53.580
They're telling me that there's a strong possibility that he's already left Europe.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.760
There's a chance that he's found his way back to Japan, then?

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.390
I suppose there is.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:01.300
What is it, sir?

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:06.930
He may have gone completely over to headquarters' side.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.630
Perhaps it's too risky to let him run loose.

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:14.970
That man hasn't been given one single piece of vital information.

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:20.240
I'll admit that he was second to none as a hunter, but in the end, that's all he's good for.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.790
Anyway, what did you need?

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:27.810
Yes, sir. About the progress of the Orbo Project that you requested the other day...

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:04.080
That's right... Sastre won't be the last.

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:07.560
Solomon will definitely send another hunter.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.830
Will I fight them? CAN I fight them?

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:17.440
The answer to that question lies within you...

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:19.700
I know that.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.950
The next hunter is in Japan?

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:38.920
An earth Craft User...

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:01.270
I wonder what's the matter?

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:04.590
Our hunt schedule is packed, so why are they just sitting around?

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:05.950
At this rate...

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:08.550
We'll just fall further and further behind.

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:11.650
I think you're right.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:19.800
Go over there and tell a joke or something to cheer them up a little.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:24.570
Are you kidding, sir?! My jokes will just make them feel even worse.

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:35.640
A hunter from HQ?

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:47.120
You think he's here to hunt Robin?

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.590
Can you think of another reason?

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:52.570
So, what is headquarters saying about him?

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:56.600
Not a word. Just that a hunter has been sent to Japan.

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:59.580
No mention at all of his name or objective.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.600
What do you suppose they're up to?

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:04.110
I guess they don't trust us anymore.

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:05.370
How do you mean?

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:07.580
You know what I mean.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:10.280
You mean the deal with Zaizen and HQ?

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:13.960
Well, I definitely get the feeling that they're not getting along.

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:15.820
You have a point.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:18.090
I guess the fact that there's no talk of cooperation...

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:21.590
...means that maybe the bosses really are on bad terms right now.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:26.490
For one thing, we could easily find Robin if we set our minds to it.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:31.730
After all, our information-gathering capability is far better than theirs in Japan.

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.940
But if it turns out that we have to help them,

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:38.680
...that'd mean that we'd take part in the hunt, wouldn't it?

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:42.080
It's almost too much to bear.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:49.660
What's the matter? Why the serious look all of a sudden?

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:52.990
Oh, I was just thinking about Amon.

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:55.860
I was wondering what he was doing there.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:09:01.070
If you're talking about the other day, it almost seemed like he was hostile to Robin, didn't it?

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:05.430
Speaking of Amon, it's really strange how he hasn't even showed up here.

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:09.100
Seriously, what's happening to this organization?

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:12.280
Hey, everyone, what are you doing?

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:14.280
Let's not sit here and mope!

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.980
Why don't we go over to Harry's for a harry's of the dog that bit ya?!

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:23.050
Um... I just meant that...

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.190
It's another cold one today. I'm calling it a day.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.920
Guess I'll go check in on her.

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:01.830
Yo!

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:06.690
What's up? You doing some shopping?

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:09.030
I was getting dinner.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:10.500
Same here.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:17.570
Isn't a getup like that just advertising that you're trying to hide your face?

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:21.110
You're tracking a Solomon hunter?

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:26.650
Sastre won't be the last. I'm sure that Solomon will send out another hunter.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:29.820
And you're trying to get the drop on him, huh?

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:34.030
But how are you gonna find a guy when you don't know his name or what he looks like?

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:35.720
Well, I...

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:38.690
You've changed.

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:44.200
It's like you'd been in a daze ever since you got here, but now you're different.

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:47.170
I'm the same as I always was.

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:50.540
It's just that up until now, I've done what Solomon told me to do.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:53.270
But from now on, I only have myself.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:58.250
I got the impression that you knew about that last hunter beforehand.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:02.290
I knew it.

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:05.160
Why don't you hit up that source again?

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:06.700
Because I...

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:10.000
It's tough to go to them because they saw you take out a hunter?

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:12.300
Huh? How did you know it was them, Nagira?

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:14.540
Why do you sound so surprised?

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.500
You'd been getting intel somehow,

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:20.430
...so it's only natural to think that you got it from your old team.

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:24.200
I'm sorry. I should have been more careful.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.710
You didn't have much choice.

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:28.640
More to the point, though, you're being too timid.

00:11:30.050 --> 00:11:32.850
Okay, so maybe they saw that you can be dangerous.

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:36.720
But it's a shame to lose all faith in your friends over a little thing like that.

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:04.020
That was quick.

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:05.380
Because I put a rush on it.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:06.720
And?

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:08.280
Just like you expected.

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:09.490
Meaning?

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:14.050
I didn't just find a man fitting his description. He entered the country under his own name.

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:15.300
His own name?!

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:19.170
Yeah. Except his ID said he was a civilian from the EU.

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:31.340
He's still at the same location?

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:02.610
Hey.

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:04.380
What are you investigating?

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.540
That hunter from yesterday.

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:08.220
And?

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:09.680
No luck whatsoever.

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:19.120
Far be it from me to tell you people not to investigate something here,

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:22.620
...but if at all possible, I'd appreciate it if you didn't forget that you have a job to do.

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:24.730
And you, Dojima...

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:29.030
What are you doing, standing around with your coat still on your arm?

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:33.570
You should have gotten down to work a long time ago.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:40.050
He's been withdrawing money on a fairly regular basis.

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:43.580
The most recent withdrawal was at the Kamiigusa branch two days ago.

00:13:44.450 --> 00:13:45.420
Something the matter?

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:50.690
No, I was just wondering why he's using his own account.

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:54.720
You were the one who said to check his bank account, Mr. Nagira.

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:59.020
Yeah, but I didn't think it would be this easy.

00:13:59.370 --> 00:14:00.890
It's almost as if...

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:05.600
It's as if he's trying to broadcast his movements.

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:21.650
What the hell is Amon thinking?

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:25.290
Why is he deliberately doing things that would leave a trail?

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:27.690
Is he calling me out?

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:31.660
No, that can't be it. Even if he was, what good would it...

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:34.830
Which means he's...

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:14.670
Okay, we're going to call it a night.

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:16.570
- Sure.
- Good work today.

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:19.080
You, too.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:08.090
Michael...

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:10.460
It's about time.

00:16:17.070 --> 00:16:18.440
It's about Amon, right?

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:20.110
Not this time.

00:16:20.110 --> 00:16:21.300
Huh? What, then?

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:25.650
Michael, have you gotten any information about a hunter from headquarters?

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:27.120
A hunter? How did you...

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:31.610
It won't end with Sastre. I'm positive they'll be sending another hunter.

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:33.720
If you get anything, let me know.

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:38.690
Robin, you aren't trying to take on HQ all by yourself, are you?

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:42.190
I'm the same person I've always been.

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:45.600
But headquarters has classified me as a Witch.

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:48.660
Is it because I learned the inner mysteries of the Craft.

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:53.130
I have to know. Otherwise, I'll...

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.110
You're tough. You know that?

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:59.440
I got some information on a hunter, all right.

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:02.080
And this time, they sent it to ME.

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:03.610
Why would headquarters do that?

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:05.090
I don't know.

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:09.750
But they were able to access my computer, so who else could it be but HQ?

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:13.020
Hm? What's the matter?

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:14.430
It wasn't them.

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:15.900
How do you mean?

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:19.060
Headquarters isn't the only one who could access your system, Michael.

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.760
I don't think so.

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:25.470
No. Amon could access it.

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:28.170
Amon? But he's...

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:07.410
Robin...

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:21.990
So, you're Robin?

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:29.430
If you insist.

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:18.540
My powers are coming back at me...!

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:22.020
This is the eternal maze.

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.060
Eternal maze?

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:30.320
Yes. The endless, black shadow which forever leads man astray.

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:10.800
Is she trapped in the Ogham ward?

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:30.090
No! This is an illusion!

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:39.230
His element... I have to sense that hunter's breath.

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:40.290
I won't be... the last!

00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:13.820
There's more to it than power.

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:18.430
As she is now, can Robin understand that...

00:22:19.830 --> 00:22:21.360
...big brother?

00:22:36.860 --> 00:22:44.850
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.670 --> 00:22:47.710
Tell me.

00:22:48.920 --> 00:22:59.700
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:09.590
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.270 --> 00:23:14.080
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.350 --> 00:23:19.450
...all those promises...

00:23:21.390 --> 00:23:25.850
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.140 --> 00:23:31.650
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:30.850 --> 00:23:40.430
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
